  "mathematics": {
    "Floor": "Only one simp unfolds original local F/S and two dsimp steps expose existing integrands. All closed-neighbor minima, 200 entries, 201 knots, zero-outside convention, singleton pullbacks, exact floor weights, denominator margins and integrability premises stay literal. Results still hold for every integer array and do not prove adopted data are recurrence outputs or carry new h248 count semantics.",
    "LogPoint": "Seven preexisting d33a proof bodies reused byte-exact; oddLoop_invariant changes only four zero/successor equation rewrites to unfolding the actual old R03 oddLoop. Q=2^80, 32 odd terms, divisor65 tail, every integer floor/ceiling, crossed denominators, negative-scale branch, exact Q zero case, reducedCheck and positive rounded-lower logI guard remain unchanged. No producer/native oracle/data replay or weaker log certificate is substituted.",
    "Child": "Existing scalar map is typed explicitly and Pi.smul_def' exposes pointwise action; a funext identity replaces failed unapplied simp_rw. The already solved single-kernel goal loses only its trailing ring. The other original proof normalizations are typed beta/cast/Fin cases or direct geometry projections. Actual target remains N at each fixed L>0; no surrogate floor(N^L), moving-L uniformity or new estimate premise.",
    "Bank_domains_and_costs": "All70 W1 windows and all36 W2 rows/three singleton/four good-pair domains retain original indices and eligibility. Both square conditions and rational kernels remain unchanged. excludedD5 remains the exact complement, its positive cost and possible unit atoms are retained separately; no unsupported D5 ordinary mass or feedback is silently kept. Labelled multiplicity and same target/coprime kernels are unchanged."
  },
